sections.content:
```html
<style>
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    grid-auto-rows: minmax(6rem, auto);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
</style>
<div class="cards">
  <article>One</article><article>Two</article><article>Three</article>
  <article>Four creates an implicit row</article>
</div>
```
The columns are explicit. The second row is implicit and receives the minmax size from grid-auto-rows.

```html
<style>
  .gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 14rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .card { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #ccd3dc; }
</style>
<section class="gallery">
  <article class="card">Alpha</article>
  <article class="card">Beta</article>
  <article class="card">Gamma</article>
</section>
```
Resize the container. Column count changes when the next usable card width no longer fits, not at a named device width.
